If you hold US-dollar cash, US securities in a non-registered account, or run USD activity through a corporation, that move carries real tax tracking implications, and the rules are not the same across account types. Personal cash conversions get a small exemption. Securities dispositions do not. Corporate accounts get no exemption at all.<br><br>
If nobody is currently tracking the adjusted cost base on that activity at the transaction level, I would be glad to take a look and flag anything worth addressing before tax season. No cost, no obligation.<br><br>
[Your Name]<br><br>
<em>This communication is for educational purposes only and does not constitute personalized investment advice.</em>
</div>
<button class="btn-copy" onclick="copyEmail(''prospect-email'', this)">Copy email</button>
</div>',
  '[{"value":"-1.7¢","label":"June CAD monthly average decline"},{"value":"70.89¢","label":"July CAD monthly average"},{"value":"$200","label":"Section 39(2) individual exemption"},{"value":"$100,000","label":"T1135 cost amount threshold"}]',
  'tax-073.jpg',
